{title: The River is Here}
{artist: Andy Park}
{key: G}

{comment: Verse 1}
[C]Down the [G]mountain the [D]river [G]flows
And it [C]brings [G]refreshing [D]wherever it [G]goes
[C]Through the [G]valleys and [D]over the [G]fields
The [C]river is [G]rushing and the [C]river is [G]here

{comment: Chorus}
The [G]river of God sets our [C]feet a-[G]dancing
The river of God fills our [C]hearts with [G]cheer
The river of God fills our [C]mouths with [G]laughter
And [C]we [G]rejoice for the [D]river is [G]here

{comment: Verse 2}
The [C]river of [G]God is [D]teeming with [G]life
And [C]all who [G]touch it can [D]be [G]revived
And [C]those who [G]linger on [D]this [G]river's shore
Will come back thirsting for more of the Lord

{comment: Verse 3}
Up to the mountain we love to go
To find the presence of the Lord
Along the banks of the river we run
We dance with laughter giving praise to the Son
